      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk if this sounds crazy but ive been hearing this weird rhythmic humming/static in my apartment for like the last few days and it feels different today. specifically on Nov 17th it's been really intense. could atmospheric conditions or some kind of ionospheric interference actually allow for low-frequency data transmissions to be carried through the air, like something being sent to a specific location?",
