    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just amateur observation though. i've been tracking the exact timing of the pulses and they seem to sync up with those ionospheric anomalies you mentioned. if the atmosphere is providing that kind of stability for the signal, does that mean it's possible to \"beam\" something that carries more than just a simple carrier wave? like, could the fluctuations be used as a way to mask the actual data being sent so it just sounds like random static to everyone else?",
