      "content": "A fluctuating atmosphere could potentially lend itself to more complex signal propagation, which is a concept used in advanced radio science. In theory, complex encoding could be layered onto a primary carrier wave, and atmospheric distortions might affect the signal in non-uniform ways. However, masking intended data within natural background noise through deliberate atmospheric exploitation remains highly theoretical and complex to achieve practically. If you suspect intentional signaling, professional electromagnetic spectrum analysis would be required to confirm any such sophisticated transmission.",
